.Sh CAVEATS
For
.Fa n
of 128 or more,
.Fn xft_memmove
always copies from high to low addresses, keeping only the first and last 64
bytes in registers.
When
.Fa dest
is below
.Fa src
and the regions overlap, bytes of
.Fa src
can be overwritten before they are read, and the result is wrong.
Sizes below 128 are safe in either direction.
.Pp
On AVX2, SSE2 and NEON,
.Fn xft_memchr
and
.Fn xft_memcmp
with
.Fa n
below the vector size load a full vector from
.Fa ptr
and discard the bytes past
.Fa n .
They may therefore read past the end of the buffer, but never into another
4 KiB page: when the vector would cross a page boundary, aligned loads that
stay in the pages holding the requested bytes are used instead.
The masked load is not instrumented by AddressSanitizer.
With AVX-512 a hardware masked load is used and nothing past
.Fa n
is read.
